        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "AVAILABLE FROM THE 23RD OF OCTOBER 2026.\r\n\r\nBorgman Earls are delighted to present this deceptively spacious three-bedroom end-of-terrace home, with the added benefit of a generous attic conversion, to the Dublin rental market.\r\n\r\nIdeally positioned on St James’s Road, the property offers excellent access to Walkinstown, Greenhills and Perrystown, combining generous living accommodation with a highly convenient and well-established residential location.\r\n\r\nThe house has been extended to the rear, creating excellent additional living and dining space, while the converted attic provides further versatile accommodation. With spacious living areas, three bedrooms, a large rear garden and off-street parking, this is a home that offers considerably more space than first impressions might suggest.\r\n\r\nThe location is particularly convenient for public transport, with the No. 9 bus route on the doorstep and several other routes within easy walking distance, including the 15a terminus and services along Greenhills Road. The M50 is also just a few minutes’ drive away, providing easy access to the wider Dublin area.\r\nA wide range of everyday amenities are close at hand, including Lidl on Greenhills Road and the nearby Greenhills Shopping Centre, with Centra, pharmacy, hairdresser and takeaway. There is also a good selection of primary and secondary schools in the surrounding area, while the extensive open space of Tymon Park is located at the end of the road. The Ashleaf and The Square Shopping Centres are also easily accessible.\r\n\r\nInternally, the accommodation begins with an entrance porch opening into the hallway, with wood flooring continuing through the main living areas.\r\nTo the front is a comfortable sitting room with fireplace and double doors opening through to a particularly spacious rear lounge, also featuring a fireplace. Beyond this, an inner hallway incorporates a useful utility area with washing machine and dryer, together with a tiled downstairs cloakroom/WC.\r\nOne of the standout features of the house is the extended kitchen and dining area to the rear. Bright and generously proportioned, it provides plenty of room for everyday family living and includes a family-sized dining table and chairs. The kitchen is fitted with a range of integrated appliances including fridge/freezer, double electric oven and hob.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are two well-proportioned double bedrooms, both offering ample built-in wardrobe space. The third bedroom is a smaller single room, while the family shower room is fitted with an electric shower.\r\nA staircase from the third bedroom leads to the spacious attic conversion, providing valuable flexible space, suitable for a variety of uses.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property benefits from a block-paved driveway to the front providing off-street parking. To the rear is a large, enclosed garden designed for ease of maintenance, together with two spacious storage sheds.\r\n\r\n300 St James’s Road offers an excellent combination of space, convenience and accessibility in a mature and popular south Dublin neighbourhood.\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended. Contact Borgman Earls to arrange an appointment."
      },
